      "description": "Watch AEK Athens FC vs Lask Linz highlights and goals from UEFA Champions League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 8, 2026. The lights of the UEFA Champions League shone brightly on September 8, 2026, as AEK Athens FC and LASK Linz prepared to battle for European supremacy. Both sides entered the pitch knowing that every tactical decision and individual effort would be scrutinized under the continental spotlight. Marin's Moment of Brilliance The match began with a palpable intensity, but it was in the 21st minute that the deadlock was broken in spectacular fashion. Razvan Marin stepped up to a direct free kick and curled a magnificent right-footed strike into the back of the net, leaving the LASK goalkeeper with no chance. Earlier, the visitors had tried their luck through Andres Andrade , but his long-range effort sailed wide. The game became increasingly physical as half-time approached, resulting in yellow cards for Marko Nikolic , Luka Jovic , and Melayro Bogarde during a period of tactical friction. VAR Intervention and Tactical Shifts The second half brought even more drama for the fans in Athens. In the 65th minute, AEK Athens thought they had secured a two-goal cushion, but the referee halted celebrations for a VAR review. After consulting the replay, the goal was revoked due to an offside position by Lovro Majer , keeping the contest on a knife-edge. LASK manager responded with tactical changes, bringing on Sasa Kalajdzic to add height to the attack, while AEK reinforced their midfield with Mijat Gacinovic . Late Drama and the Final Whistle The closing stages were a test of nerves for the home side. Deep into stoppage time, Sasa Kalajdzic had a golden opportunity to snatch a point, but his close-range header somehow missed the target. A late defensive blunder by Alberto Brignoli almost gifted LASK an opening, but the Greek defense recovered just in time. Despite LASK finishing with 51% of the possession, the final whistle confirmed a vital victory for AEK Athens on a night where Marin ’s set-piece excellence proved decisive."
